{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to apply the user's decisions on each group. If a decision adds an obligation that no reviewer saw, the skill MUST direct them to review that group again before asking for agreement.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The requirement text, \"The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to apply the user's decisions on each group. If a decision adds an obligation that no reviewer saw, the skill MUST direct them to review that group again before asking for agreement\", prescribes no library, algorithm, signature, type, field or delegation through a named interface. Every clause is about what the skill document tells agents to do. Any document that gave the same directions would satisfy it, whatever its layout or wording, so no structural obligation needs implementation evidence.\n\nThe supplied root, `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, does carry the directive in `section[Habeas requirements]/section[Workflow]`, step 4. It says: \"Apply the user's decisions. If a decision adds an obligation no reviewer saw, review that group again.\" The Gate that follows it forbids implementation until the user has agreed to, rejected or deferred every group. That places the re-review before asking for agreement. Whether the skill's wording is adequate is a behavioral question, not a structural gap.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has three obligations on the `habeas-requirements` skill text. It must direct agents to apply the user's decisions on each group. It must direct a re-review of the group when a decision adds an obligation no reviewer saw. That re-review must come before asking for agreement.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_rereviews_a_group_a_decision_extends]` covers all three. It reads the skill's workflow step that contains \"Present each group to the user\" through `step`, `step_of` and `workflow_steps`. `workflow_steps` collapses wrapped lines, so the phrases match the wrapped text in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`. It then calls `assert_text_in_order` to require, in this order:\n- \"Apply the user's decisions\". This covers the first obligation.\n- \"If a decision adds an obligation no reviewer saw, review that group again\". This covers both the trigger and the action of the second obligation.\n- \"**Gate:**\". This is the point where agreement is required, so it covers the third obligation, that the re-review precedes asking for agreement.\n\nIf the re-review sentence were removed, reworded, or moved after the Gate, the test would fail. The skill is static text, so a phrase-presence and ordering assertion is the only observable behaviour to test. I found no further behavioural obligation or boundary case that is untested.",
